;; manifest/origin-domains.edn — the origin plane's DATA.
;;
;; The RULE lives in manifest/repository-rules.edn (:vocabulary/id :origin).
;; This file holds only the fact the rule needs: for a repository that
;; implements someone else's specification or product, WHAT DOMAIN does that
;; authority actually use.
;;
;; Everything else is derived. `com-` was never a semantic category meaning
;; "commercial company" — it is what stripe.com reverses to. Nothing about a
;; repository is classified here; a domain is recorded and the prefix falls
;; out of it (ADR-2608040100).
;;
;; Direction matters: prefix is derived FROM domain, never parsed back OUT of a
;; name. `com-yang-ming-api` cannot be split into a domain because a label may
;; itself contain no hyphen while the subject does. The check is one-way —
;; "does the repository name start with the derived prefix".
;;
;; Coverage is partial and stated as such. A domain absent from this file means
;; UNVERIFIED, never CONFORMANT: silence must not read as a pass.

{:schema "kotoba.origin-domains.v1"
 :authority "90-docs/adr/2608040100-origin-plane-is-reverse-dns-of-the-real-domain.edn"

 :derivation
 {:steps ["take the authority's registrable domain (drop www and any host label"
          " that carries no separate NS delegation — ec.europa.eu is recorded"
          " as europa.eu, unstats.un.org as un.org)"
          "split on '.'"
          "reverse the label order"
          "join with '-'  => the derived prefix"
          "the repository name must equal the derived prefix, or begin with"
          " the derived prefix followed by '-' and a subject"]
  :examples {"stripe.com"            "com-stripe"
             "ietf.org"              "org-ietf   (org-ietf-x509)"
             "libp2p.io"             "io-libp2p  (io-libp2p-specs-kad-dht)"
             "ipfs.tech"             "tech-ipfs  (tech-ipfs-specs-ipns)"
             "berkeley.edu"          "edu-berkeley (edu-berkeley-spice)"
             "protobuf.dev"          "dev-protobuf"
             "sel4.systems"          "systems-sel4"
             "digital.go.jp"         "jp-go-digital (jp-go-digital-design-system)"
             "boj.or.jp"             "jp-or-boj"}
  :note "The examples above are not aspirational. Every one except sel4.systems
         and boj.or.jp is an existing conformant repository name, which is the
         evidence that this rule is already the de-facto convention and only
         lacked a written form and a verifier."}

 ;; DNS evidence: every domain below returned NS records (or, for the two host
 ;; labels noted in :derivation, an A record under a delegated parent) on this
 ;; date. That proves the domain exists and is delegated — it does NOT prove the
 ;; domain belongs to the authority the repository implements. That second claim
 ;; rests on assistant knowledge and owner review, and is recorded as such
 ;; rather than dressed up as a measurement.
 :dns-checked-at "2026-08-04"
 :dns-checked-by "dig +short NS <domain>, 68 domains, 68 delegated"
 :authority-binding-evidence :asserted-not-measured

